  "plain": "A physicist who has worked on government advanced-research projects, Eric Davis, says on a podcast hosted by Jesse Michels that an aviation journalist named Bill Sweetman did a deep investigation in the 1980s, after Ronald Reagan became president. Davis says Sweetman looked at special access programs, highly secret government projects that only a few cleared people may know about, and how they were split into sealed compartments and sometimes duplicated one another. It matters to the story because such hidden structures are where secret UFO work could supposedly be kept."
